Is to ascertain whether carbetocin is more effective in reducing bleeding after the delivery of the baby during a planned ceasarean section compared with the current management which uses syntocinon and ergometrine.

Intervention Arm: Carbotencin; 
Active Comparator: Oxytocin and ergometrine; 

Study is estimated to enrol 600 participants, and will take place at hospitals in the United Kingdom.

Trial terminated: Study prematurely ended due to change in clinical practice during recruitment (which was much slower than anticipated): Standard care no longer comprised syntocinon plus ergometrine.
